{"name":"Shy Time","hex":"#ddac9a","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Tachawit. The native name for the Shawiya language."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Easily frightened; timid.","Reserved; disinclined to familiar approach."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shy"},{"term":"time","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The inevitable progression into the future with the passing of present and past events.","The feeling of the passage of events and their relative duration, as experienced by an individual."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To measure or record the time, duration, or rate of something.","To choose when something commences or its duration."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/time"}],"entries":[{"title":"Time","blocks":[{"text":"Time is the continuous progression of existence that occurs in an apparently irreversible succession from the past, through the present, and into the future. Time dictates all forms of action, age, and causality, being a component quantity of various measurements used to sequence events, to compare the duration of events or the intervals between them, and to quantify rates of change of quantities in material reality or in conscious experience. Time is often referred to as the fourth dimension and the temporal dimension, in addition to the three spatial dimensions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/MontreGousset001.jpg/330px-MontreGousset001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time","wikidata":"Q11471"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/MontreGousset001.jpg/500px-MontreGousset001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/MontreGousset00